# Threadline Prospect Qualification Scorecard

Score only to prioritise outreach; do not pretend the number measures objective fit.

## Strong-fit checks
- Proven offer around GBP 5k+ or customer LTV that makes a GBP 2.5k-5k monthly fee economically sensible.
- Established B2B consultant, specialist agency or expert-led service firm.
- Founder/expert credibility materially influences acquisition.
- Capacity to accept more demand.
- Visible content potential.
- Content is already attempted or strongly believed in.
- Clear signs of positioning/creative/operational pain.
- Willing to record and approve.

## Disqualifiers
- Pre-revenue / unclear offer.
- Low-ticket economics with no credible volume engine.
- Wants guaranteed virality or guaranteed revenue.
- Will not record or provide expertise.
- Expects Threadline to invent proof/expertise.
- Procurement complexity disproportionate to founding-stage Threadline.
- Wants a bespoke software fork.

